## 7. Plano do bootstrap (scripts/aws-bootstrap.sh SEM --apply: só imprime)
conta=<ACCOUNT_ID> região=us-east-2 role=devfinder-laravel-github-deploy apply=0
[plano] aws iam create-open-id-connect-provider --url https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com --client-id-list sts.amazonaws.com
[plano] aws iam create-role --role-name devfinder-laravel-github-deploy --assume-role-policy-document file://TMP/deploy-role-trust.json --description Depl
[plano] aws iam put-role-policy --role-name devfinder-laravel-github-deploy --policy-name deploy --policy-document file://TMP/deploy-role.json
[plano] aws budgets create-budget --account-id <ACCOUNT_ID> --budget file://TMP/budget.json --notifications-with-subscribers file://TMP/no

Depois: no GitHub, Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions:
  variável AWS_DEPLOY_ROLE_ARN = arn:aws:iam::<ACCOUNT_ID>:role/devfinder-laravel-github-deploy   (não é segredo)
  secret   DIRECT_DATABASE_URL = URL direta do Neon (só para o migrate)

